# SYNOPSIS

```usage
winsrv
```

# DESCRIPTION

`winsrv` is the window server (docs/21, 03 §4-5).
It holds the output as displayd(8)'s one client, a session of the display engine protocol (docs/proto/display.md §1a), and composites the screen on the CPU into two buffers of its own: while one is on screen the other is drawn, its damage only, and flipped in by an APPLY.
A buffer it applied is busy until a vblank shows a newer stamp.

The output's frame clock is displayd's VBLANK: each one says which stamp is on screen, and a Counter rises with it.

Windows (M7 step 7d1b, docs/proto/wsys.md): an attach with the aname `new -dx W -dy H` makes a window, and its directory is the attach's root, the app's `/wsys/self`; an empty aname is the whole tree.
Opening a window's `surface` gives its channel, on which the app attaches vx-buffers and presents them: a present costs a credit, each frame event gives back what was composited, and feedback says when it reached the screen.
At each vblank a present whose acquire point has come is latched: its damage copied into the window's own backing and its release point signalled at once (release at composite).
The screen is composited from the backings, bottom to top, over the desk.
A window lives while a fid holds a node of it or its channel is open.
Input and focus are 7d1c's.
It starts with `vx.display` and `vx.desktop` on the kernel command line (boot/svc/display.ndb).

# FILES

: `/wsys/info`
  An ndb(6) record: the protocol's `version`, the `output`, its `width` and `height`, and the `frames` its clock has counted.
: `/wsys/outputs/`
  Where displayd's tree is mounted.
: `/wsys/windows/N/ctl`
  `move X Y`, `resize W H`, `title TEXT`, `raise`, `close`.
: `/wsys/windows/N/info`
  The window: `id`, `title`, `x`, `y`, `width`, `height`, `config` (its configure sequence), `presented`, `dropped`.
: `/wsys/windows/N/frame`
  Its last frame event and feedback, as text.
: `/wsys/windows/N/surface`
  Opened with 9Px's srv extension: the window's channel, one app's at a time.

